{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ModifiedContent\/defaultPosition(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"position"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","text":"UnitPoint"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","text":"Scene","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP"},{"kind":"text","text":"\n"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"position","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","type":"reference"},{"text":" that specifies where to place a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"newly opened window relative to the screen bounds.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A scene that uses a default position for new windows.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The first time your app opens a window from a particular scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration, the system places the window at the center of the screen by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default. For scene types that support multiple simultaneous windows, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system offsets each additional window by a small amount to avoid","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"completely obscuring existing windows.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can override the default placement of the first window by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applying a scene modifier that indicates where to place the window","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative to the screen bounds. For example, you can request that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system place a new window in the bottom trailing corner of the screen:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","        }","        .defaultPosition(.bottomTrailing)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The system aligns the point in the window that corresponds to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with the point in the screen that corresponds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the same unit point."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You typically use one of the predefined unit points — like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomTrailing"},{"text":" in the above example — but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you can also use a custom unit point. For example, the following","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"modifier aligns the point that’s one quarter of the way from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leading edge of the window with the point that’s one quarter of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the way from the leading edge of the screen, while centering the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"window in the y-dimension:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["WindowGroup {","    ContentView()","}",".defaultPosition(UnitPoint(x: 0.25, y: 0.5))"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The modifier affects any scene type that creates windows in macOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"namely:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Window"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DocumentGroup"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Settings"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The value that you provide acts only as an initial default. During state","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restoration, the system restores the window to the position that it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last occupied.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets a default position for a window."}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5ScenePAAE15defaultPositionyQrAA9UnitPointVF::SYNTHESIZED::s:11OpenSwiftUI15ModifiedContentV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","text":"UnitPoint"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","text":"Scene"}],"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"title":"defaultPosition(_:)"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/modifiedcontent\/defaultposition(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ModifiedContent"]]},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/UnitPoint":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/unitpoint","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","type":"topic","title":"UnitPoint","abstract":[{"text":"A normalized 2D point in a view’s coordinate space.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/ModifiedContent/defaultPosition(_:)":{"title":"defaultPosition(_:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets a default position for a window."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ModifiedContent\/defaultPosition(_:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/modifiedcontent\/defaultposition(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultPosition"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","text":"UnitPoint"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","text":"Scene"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/docum